{"name":"Cockatrice Brown","hex":"#a46422","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cockatrice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of basilisk, a serpentine dragon so poisonous that even its gaze is deadly. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A monster with a lethal gaze or breath, originally believed to originate from a cock egg brooded over by a snake or toad, later specifically combining serpentine and landfowl features and particularly  a rooster-headed wyvern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cockatrice"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cockatrice","blocks":[{"text":"A cockatrice is a mythical beast, essentially a two-legged dragon, wyvern, or serpent-like creature with a rooster's head. Described by Laurence Breiner as \"an ornament in the drama and poetry of the Elizabethans\", it was featured prominently in English thought and myth for centuries. According to legend, they are created by a chicken egg hatched by a toad or snake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/DragonTransom.jpg/330px-DragonTransom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockatrice"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org